$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(tert-Butylthio)-N-(2,6-dimethylphenyl)-5-nitrobenzamide (5a). Amide
(4a) (6.43 mmol; 1.96 g) was added to the solution of tert-butylthiol
(7.72 mmol; 0.70 g; 0.5 ml) and sodium hydroxide (7,07 mmol; 0.28 g) in
DMF (10 ml) at 0°C. It was stirred at 0°C for 3h. After that
tert-butylthiol (20 mol%) was added and it was stirred for another 0.5h.
The mixture was poured in to the ice cold 5% hydrochloric acid, the
precipitated solid was filtered and washed with water. After drying pure
tert-butythiolether was obtained as a yellowish crystalline solid in 96%
yield (2.20 g).
2-(tert-Butylthio)-N-(2,6-dimethylphenyl)-5-nitrobenzamide (5a), yield
(2.20 g), 96% M.p.192-194°C (ethanol). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.82
(d, J= 2.6, 1H), 8.54 (br s, 1H), 8.24 (dd, J= 2.6, 8.5, 1H), 7.82 (d, J=
8.5, 1H), 7.19 - 7.08 (m, 3H), 2.35 (s, 6H), 1.40 (s, 9H). 13C NMR
(101MHz, DMSO): δ 164.7, 146.3, 143.9 ,140.0, 136.6, 135.5, 134.4 ,
127.8, 126.8, 123.5, 121.9. IR (KBr): 3244 m (NH), 2967 w (CH3), 1651 s
(CONH), 1531 s (CONH), 1510 s (NO2), 1396 w (CH3), 1346 s (NO2), 1317 m
(CONH) cm-1 . Anal. calcd for C19H22N2O3S: C, 63.66; H, 6.19; N, 7.81.
Found: C, 63.58; H, 5.96; N, 7.60.
