$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(Cyclopentylthio)-3-iodo-5-methylbenzene (30) A mixture of
1,3-diiodo-5-methylbenzene (29) (2.00 g, 5.81 mmol),
tris(dibenzylideneacetone) dipalladium (0) (20 mg, 0.027 mmol),
bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene (22 mg, 0.04 mmol), triethylamine (1.5
mL, 11 mmol) and 1-methyl-2-pyrrolidinone (3 mL) were stirred at 20 °C
under nitrogen for 1 h. Cyclopentanethiol (0.15 mL, 1.45 mmol) was added
and the mixture was heated to 60 °C for 18 h. The mixture was cooled to
20 °C and was diluted with phosphate buffer solution (pH 6.5) and water.
The mixture was extracted with EtOAc and the organic phase was dried
(Na2SO4). The solvent was evaporated in vacuo and the residue was
purified by chromatography on FlashmasterTM (silica, 70 g) eluting with
cyclohexane to give 30 Yield 444 mg, 96%. 1H NMR δ (CDCl3) 7.48 (1H, br
s), 7.34 (1H, br s), 7.10 (1H, br s), 3.62 -3.55 (1H, m), 2.27 (3H, s),
2.12 -2.02 (2H, m), 1.84 -1.73 (4H, m), 1.67 -1.59 (2H, m).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered solution used (phosphate buffer) (stage 3)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Rapidly Metabolized, Long-Acting β2 Adrenergic Receptor
Agonist with a Short Onset Time Incorporating a Sulfone Group Suitable
for Once-Daily Dosing
