$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM phenyl-3-tolylsulfide 3-Bromotoluene (3.55 mL, 29.23 mmol, 1.0 equiv),
2-propanol (30 ml), potassium hydroxide1 (3.80 g, 58.47 mmol, 2.0 equiv),
tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (169 mg, 0.146 mmol, 0.005
equiv), (S)-BINAP (182 mg., 0.292 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and benzenethiol (3.0
mL, 29.23 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a nitrogen atmosphere for
20-22 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was completed it was cooled (<30 °C)
and quenched with water (30 mL) which resulted in a small exotherm (~6
°C) and formation of an oil. The resultant mixture was allowed to stir
for 1 h at 10-15 °C. Adjusted to ~pH 7 with concentrated HCl, separated
the oil. Re dissolved oil in ethyl acetate, extracted with water, then
brine and dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, concentrated to
dryness. Obtained a red oil2, 5.6 g. phenyl-3-tolylsulfide, Yield 96% m/z
200; C13H12S requires: C, 77.95; H, 6.04; S, 16.0. Found: C, 77.6; H,
5.92; S, 16.4%; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.23 (m, 9H), 2.31 (s, 3H);
IR (cm-1) νmax; 1591, 1582, 1476, 1439.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Migita reaction
