$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4'-methylphenylsulfanyl)benzoic acid (4b) [17]. Following a modified
procedure by I. K. Kostakis,[3] a mixture of 2- ethyliodobenzoate (5.52
g, 20 mmol, 1.0 eq.), 4-methylthiophenol (2.98 g, 24 mmol, 1.2 eq.),
K2CO3 (3.6 g, 26 mmol, 1.3 eq.), Cu powder (0.64 g, 10 mmol, 0.5 eq.) and
KI (1.66 g, 10 mmol, 0.5 eq.) in 25 mL DMF were stirred at 110 °C for 24
h. The reaction was quenched through the addition of H2O and the mixture
was extracted with EtOAc three times. The combined organic layers were
dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The
crude product was purified by flash chromatography (silica gel,
pentane/EtOAc = 50/1) to obtain the pure desired ester in 95% (5.18 g, 19
mmol) yield as a colorless oil. 95% (5.18 g, 19 mmol) yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Direct Arylation of Benzoic Acids by
Tandem Decarboxylation/C-H Activation
