$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-(arylsulfinyl)benzene via SNAr reaction
followed by oxidation4 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-(phenylsulfinyl)benzene 1b.
Amixture of 1-bromo-2-fluoro-5-acetyl-benzene (1.5 g, 7.1 mmol),
benzenethiol (1.0 g, 7.0 mmol), K2CO3 (1.1 g, 7.9 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was
heated to 160 ◦C for 2 h in a closed vial. After cooling to ambient
temperature the mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (10 mL), washed
(water, brine), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vaccuo. Purrification
by column chromatography (solvent: c-hexane : ethyl acetate = 1 : 1)
afforded the corresponding thioether. dark red oil (2.2 g, 7.1 mmol,
&gt;95 %). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ= 8.09 (d, J = 1.5Hz, 1H), 7.64 (dd,
J = 8.5, 1.5Hz, 1H), 7.58-7.53 (m, 2H), 7.49-7.45 (m, 3H), 6.72 (d, J =
8.5Hz, 1H), 2.52 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 75MHz): δ= 196, 147.2,
135.5, 135.2, 132.7, 130.7, 130.0, 127.4, 120.7, 26.5 ppm. MS (EI): m/z =
306.0, 308.0. IR (ATR): ev = 3078 (w), 1669 (s), 1581 (s), 1273 (s), 1225
(s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM closed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
