$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthetic Procedure of
4,4'-Bis(p-tolylthio)biphenyl (3b). To a solution of Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 4
mol %) and Xantphos (12.1 mg, 4.2 mol %) in DMF (1.0 mL) was added
4,4'-dibromo-1,1'-biphenyl (156 mg, 0.5 mmol) in DMF (0.5 mL) at 25 °C
under nitrogen atmosphere. After being stirred for 5 min, (4-Me-C6H4S)3In
(164.7 mg, 0.34 mmol) and DIPEA (87.0 μL, 0.5 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL) was
transferred via double-ended needle, and the mixture was stirred at 100
°C for 4 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with NaHCO3 (satd aq). The
aqueous layer was extracted with ether (3x20 mL), and the combined
organic layers were washed with water and brine, dried with MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to give 3b (167.4 mg, 84%)
as white solid. 2,4-Di(4-methoxyphenylthio)-1-methoxybenzene (3d): white
solid, yield 95% mp 79 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.35 (d, J = 8.69
Hz, 2H), 7.20 (d, J = 8.88 Hz, 2H), 7.02 (d, J = 8.42 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J
= 8.69 Hz, 2H), 6.77 (d, J = 8.88 Hz, 2H), 6.75 (d, J = 8.42 Hz, 1H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 160.2, 159.3, 154.2, 136.5, 133.9, 129.3, 129.1,
128.5, 127.7, 125.8, 121.5, 115.1, 114.7, 110.8, 56.0, 55.3; IR (film)
3435, 1592, 1493, 1288 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd for C21H20O3S2 m/z 384.0854
[M+], found m/z 384.0850.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Di-, Tri-, and Tetrasulfides through Multifold Carbon-Sulfur
Cross-Coupling Reactions with Indium Tri(organothiolates) in a One-Pot
Procedure
