$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-((3-methoxyphenyl)sulfinyl)benzene 1g A mixture of
1-bromo-2-fluoro-5-acetyl-benzene (1.5 g, 6.8 mmol),
3-methoxybenzenethiol (0.9 g, 6.7 mmol), K2CO3 (1.0 g, 7.4 mmol) in DMF
(5 mL) was heated to 160 ◦C for 2 h in a closed vial. After cooling to
ambient temperature the mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (10 mL),
washed (water, brine), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vaccuo.
Purrification by column chromatography (solvent: c-hexane : ethyl acetate
= 2 : 1) afforded the corresponding thioether. yellow oil (2.2 g, 6.7
mmol, &gt;95 %). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ= 8.89 (d, J = 1.8Hz, 1H), 7.64
(dd, J = 8.3Hz, 1H), 7.37 (dd, J = 8.2, 8.0Hz, 1H), 7.13 (dd, J = 7.5,
1.8Hz, 1H), 7.09-7.07 (m, 1H), 7.00 (dd, J = 8.0, 2.0Hz, 1H), 6.78 (d, J
= 8.3Hz, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 2.52 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 75MHz): δ=
196.5, 152.8, 150.0, 143.3, 140.6, 138.7, 136.5, 130.2, 129.3, 128.0,
122.2, 121.6, 114.7, 27.0 ppm. MS (EI): m/z = 336.0, 338.0. IR (ATR): ev
= 3072 (w), 2977 (w), 2841 (w), 1669 (s), 1577 (s), 1245 (s), 1228 (s),
1022 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM closed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
