$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-((4-trifluoromethylphenyl)sulfinyl)benzene 1h A
mixture of 1-bromo-2-fluoro-5-acetyl-benzene (1.2 g, 5.7 mmol),
4-(trifluoromethyl)benzenethiol (1.0 g, 5.6 mmol), K2CO3 (0.9 g, 6.4
mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was heated to 160 ◦C for 2 h in a closed vial. After
cooling to ambient temperature the mixture was diluted with diethyl ether
(10 mL), washed (water, brine), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vaccuo.
Purrification by column chromatography (solvent: c-hexane : ethyl acetate
= 2 : 1) afforded the corresponding thioether. yellow oil (2.1 g, 5.6
mmol, &gt;95 %). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ= 8.15 (s, 1H), 7.72 (d, J =
8.6Hz, 1H), 7.67 (d, J = 8.3Hz, 1H), 7.58 (d, J = 8.3Hz, 1H), 6.94 (d, J
= 8.3Hz, 1H), 2.55 (s, 3H) ppm. MS (EI): m/z = 374.2, 376.2. IR (ATR): ev
= 3099 (w), 3004 (w), 1679 (s), 1581 (s), 1317 (s), 1242 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM closed vial used
