$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-((4-trifluoromethoxyphenyl)sulfinyl)benzene 1i A
mixture of 1-bromo-2-fluoro-5-acetyl-benzene (1.5 g, 7.1 mmol),
4-(trifluoromethoxy)benzenethiol (1.3 g, 7.0 mmol), K2CO3 (1.0 g, 7.9
mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was heated to 160 ◦C for 2 h in a closed vial. After
cooling to ambient temperature the mixture was diluted with diethyl ether
(10 mL), washed (water, brine), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vaccuo.
Purrification by column chromatography (solvent: c-hexane : ethyl acetate
= 2 : 1) afforded the corresponding thioether. red solid (2.6 g, 6.7
mmol, &gt;95 %). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ= 8.08 (d, J = 1.8Hz, 1H), 7.63
(dd, J = 8.2, 1.8Hz, 1H), 7.38-7.34 (m, 3H), 7.31-7.25 (m, 1H), 6.72 (d,
J = 8.3Hz, 1H), 2.52 (s, 3H), 2.38 (s, 3H) ppm. 13CNMR (CDCl3, 75MHz): δ=
195.8, 162.0, 147.3, 140.1, 135.9, 134.9, 134.2, 132.5, 132.4, 130.6,
129.9, 129.5, 127.2, 126.7, 120.4, 116.7, 26.3 ppm. m. p.: 61 ◦C
(c-hexane/ethyl acetate). IR (ATR): ev = 3072 (w), 3024 (w), 2916 (w),
1679 (s), 1581 (s), 1384 (s), 1262 (s), 1222 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM closed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Direct Arylation of 2-Bromo-diaryl
Sulfoxides via C-H Bond Activation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wesch, Thomas; Berthelot-Brehier, Anais; Leroux, Frederic R.; Colobert,
Francoise
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(10), 2490-2493

