$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-Chlorodibenzo[b,f]thiepin-10(11H)-one (9a). 4-Chlorothiophenol (20.45
g, 141.4 mmol) was added to a solution of KOH (26.0 g, 472 mmol) in water
(270 mL). The solution was heated to 50°C, and copper powder (2.61 g,
41.8 mmol) was added, followed by 2-iodophenylacetic acid (35.3 g, 135
mmol). The mixture was refluxed for 24 h under stirring, cooled, and
filtrated. The filtrate was acidified with 2 M HCl (20 mL), and EtOAc
(250 mL) was added. The phases were separated, and the aqueous phase was
extracted with EtOAc (5 x 250 mL). The combined organic phases were
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), and concentrated to give 35.6 g (95%)
of 2-(2-((4-chlorophenyl)thio)phenyl)acetic acid as a light yellow solid.
2-(2-((4-chlorophenyl)thio)phenyl)acetic acid, 35.6 g (95%) yield LC-MS:
ELSD, 92.1%; UV, 93.2%; M+, 278.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
